// Topbar tabs: „Datei“ and „Seite“ open a dropdown over the page (.tab-menu) that closes after a choice, a click elsewhere or Esc; „Zeichnen“ and „Kommentieren“ show their own tool bar (#toolbox-draw/#toolbox-comment, tapping the open tab again hides it). A bar is docked left (vertical), docked top (horizontal) or free; dragging the grip moves it and it snaps to the left/top edge, a double tap on the grip switches between one line and a nearly square grid. Dock, position and layout are kept per bar in localStorage. A tool button selects the tool on the first tap; tapping the active tool again opens #tool-pop with its settings: the style controls live there in sections (.pop-section) that are switched on per button via data-pop. Shapes and text markup are one button each (data-group) that remembers the last kind.
